WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
Goujian, King of Yue, was once defeated by Fuchai, King of Wu.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.942
His country grew weak, and he himself suffered great humiliation.

00:00:06.292 --> 00:00:12.220
After returning to Yue, Goujian did not give up hope.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.170
He resolved to sleep on brushwood and taste gall, reminding himself to rise again.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.472
He told himself he must never forget today's humiliation.

00:00:19.822 --> 00:00:23.590
He slept on brushwood, not letting himself live too comfortably.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.588
Every day he tasted the bitter gall, remembering the pain of defeat.

00:00:27.938 --> 00:00:31.226
The bitterness made him frown — and made him even more clear-headed.

00:00:31.576 --> 00:00:34.624
Goujian labored alongside the people and set the country in order.

00:00:34.974 --> 00:00:38.334
Yue's population and grain grew year by year.

00:00:38.684 --> 00:00:42.332
Many years passed, and Yue's strength slowly recovered.

00:00:42.682 --> 00:00:45.802
Goujian waited patiently, preparing for the final opportunity.

00:00:46.152 --> 00:00:49.560
The soldiers' morale rose higher and higher, ready to set out.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.478
In the end, Yue finally defeated Wu.

00:00:52.828 --> 00:00:56.788
"Sleeping on brushwood and tasting gall" reminds us that only perseverance brings hope.

00:00:57.138 --> 00:01:00.786
This idiom became a symbol of persevering to the very end.

